A PhD Researcher Continues to Describe Torture Account and US Normalized Violence of Voice Insertion

“How on earth are they doing this?! With what technology?”

L’Enfant Plaza

By now, Pearson knows about the “invisibility” element campaign behind his torture. In his apartment and public spaces, it has been technology that moves him to places and inserts thoughts, dreams, and images. He has written about it in graphic detail. There has also been the street theater, including a Black man with “Die” in bold white letters on a black T-shirt waiting for Pearson to arrive at his regular outdoors spot for writing. “It’s the plausible deniability that is characteristic, but it was often patterned — white Impact font on a black T-shirt. So much for the deniability part when much of the street theater is in identical attire.”

